[{"id":"D1-0001","d":1,"o":"1.9","x":"medium","q":"A risk assessment identifies a threat with high impact but very low likelihood. Mitigating it would cost substantially more than the expected loss. Which risk response is MOST appropriate?","c":["Accept the risk and document the decision","Transfer the risk through insurance","Mitigate the risk regardless of cost","Ignore the risk since likelihood is low"],"k":""},{"id":"D1-0002","d":1,"o":"1.10","x":"easy","q":"A development team is threat modeling a new payment service and wants a structured way to enumerate potential threats against each element of the data-flow diagram. Which approach BEST supports this goal?","c":["Apply STRIDE categories to each data-flow element","Score each known vulnerability using CVSS","Commission an external penetration test","Review the enterprise risk register entries"],"k":""},{"id":"D1-0003","d":1,"o":"1.6","x":"easy","q":"An internal document states that all company laptops MUST use AES-256 full-disk encryption. Compliance is mandatory and no exceptions are listed. Which type of document is this?","c":["A security standard","A security policy","A security guideline","A security procedure"],"k":""},{"id":"D1-0004","d":1,"o":"1.1","x":"medium","q":"During an internal audit, a CISSP-certified analyst discovers that a colleague has been falsifying vulnerability scan results to hide missed remediation deadlines. What should the analyst do FIRST?","c":["Confront the colleague privately and ask them to stop","Report the findings through the organization's internal channels","File an ethics complaint with ISC2 against the colleague","Escalate directly to the external audit committee"],"k":""},{"id":"D1-0005","d":1,"o":"1.4","x":"easy","q":"A US-based SaaS provider hosts and processes EU customer personal data strictly on the instructions of its European business clients. Under the GDPR, how is the provider classified?","c":["As a data processor","As a data controller","As a data subject","As a supervisory authority"],"k":""},{"id":"D1-0006","d":1,"o":"1.7","x":"medium","q":"An organization is beginning its business continuity program. Management wants to know which business processes and systems must be recovered first after a disruption. Which activity provides this answer?","c":["A quantitative risk assessment","A disaster recovery test","A business impact analysis","A threat and vulnerability assessment"],"k":""},{"id":"D1-0007","d":1,"o":"1.11","x":"medium","q":"A manufacturer learns that a vulnerable open-source library may be embedded in firmware delivered by several of its third-party suppliers. Which practice gives the organization the BEST visibility into this exposure?","c":["Signing non-disclosure agreements with every supplier","Increasing the frequency of internal code reviews","Purchasing cyber insurance covering supply chain incidents","Requiring a software bill of materials from each supplier"],"k":""},{"id":"D1-0008","d":1,"o":"1.2","x":"hard","q":"An online contract platform must ensure that a customer who electronically signs an agreement cannot later credibly deny having signed it. Which security concept is the platform enforcing, and what typically provides it?","c":["Authenticity, provided by validating the customer's login credentials","Nonrepudiation, provided by digital signatures over the agreement","Integrity, provided by hashing the agreement after signature","Accountability, provided by recording the signing in an audit log"],"k":""}]
